# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Human-only review paths
#
# CI cannot catch the failure modes here, so a green build is not evidence that
# these changes are safe. They need a person to look.
#
# - Dependency graph (lockfile, mobile package.json, native-deps.json): a JS-only
#   dependency change can silently re-key the Expo native module graph onto a
#   second React/react-native instance, which blanks native video and GIF
#   rendering on a real device while typecheck, tests, and the bundle all pass.
#   See docs/architecture/ADR-013-mobile-versioning-and-ota-updates.md.
# - Auth: a regression locks people out or lets the wrong people in, and tests
#   assert the code's behaviour rather than the policy it should encode.
# - Billing / finance: moves real money. Wrong is expensive and hard to unwind.
# - Migrations: run once against production data. There is no second attempt.
#
# NOTE: last matching pattern wins in CODEOWNERS, so these override the
# defaults above. Enforcement additionally requires "Require review from Code
# Owners" on the branch protection rule for main.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Dependency graph / native safety (ADR-013)
/pnpm-lock.yaml @lilseyi
/apps/mobile/package.json @lilseyi
